Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 53 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  1   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN MANY AREAS  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  10    3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  The tumor is 1 2cm in diameter in histologic section  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The in situ component is present both within the infiltrating tumor and in sections separate from it  Immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  RIGHT  2   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   50   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  50    COMEDO TYPE  NOTE  The infiltrating tumor in this specimen is 0 8cm in diameter in histologic section  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass  is a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one of the bulbous ends  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two yellow firm nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm in average size and focal gritty areas  one present around stitched tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Stitch area submitted in A and B  remainder submitted in C through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   2  is a 3 x 2 x 0 4cm mass of fibrofatty tissue  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue  fat  and a subtle faint nodularity  No frozen done  Specimen submitted entirely in K through N  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS AREAS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS AREAS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  WHITE 10 REPORTS TO  Bradley T Hyman  M D  Alik Farber  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B  RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Absent.
