om the aforementioned lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink ill defined nodular area  1 5cm from the posterior margin  and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  The combined overall maximal dimension of tumor is about 5cm  The remainder of the parenchyma is unremarkable with sectioning of the axillary aspect revealing no lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to anterior and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma between lesions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined nodular area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma  lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of firm  nodular mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  skin right breast   are three irregular portions of tan pink skin with attached tan pink fibrofatty tissue  The fragments measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  Also received in the specimen container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm aggregate of tan pink fibrofatty tissue  Sectioning reveals no gross abnormalities  and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND 1A  RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cell