Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  1   FORMING TWO NODULES EACH ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  INVOLVING MANY DUCTS AND LOBULES IN ALL SECTIONS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel is not seen  The margins appear free of invasive carcinoma  The intra operative macroscopic impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 94 at 07 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  firm  yellow tan fibrofatty tissue with a wire and x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal multiple 0 05cm tan  pale calcifications and fibrosis  Sections with calcifications submitted in cassettes A through C  remaining tissue is submitted entirely in cassettes D through F  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST MASS   NO GROSSLY EVIDENT MALIGNANT TUMOR  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST MASS   report_end  , Present.
