Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Adriana Dionigi Corben  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Left breast re excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  SEVERAL FOCI OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH COMEDONECROSIS  INVOLVING 8 OF 11 TISSUE BLOCKS  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   3  HEALING SURGICAL SITE  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  HEALING SURGICAL SITE WITH NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm portion of gray white to tan red fibrofatty tissue  with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focally dense gray white fibrous tissue  with hemorrhage surrounding the previous surgical site  Also noted is chalky yellow discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  The hemorrhage and fat necrosis come to 0 2cm of the inked resection margin  No discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast anterior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fat necrosis with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday May 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 28 26AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left  Inferior Margin   Excision PART B  Breast  Left  Anterior Margin   Excision  report_end  , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 AUG 93 at 15 21 CLINICAL DATA  Right mammographic abnormality                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  85   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    NOTE  The carcinoma measures 0 7cm in greatest dimension  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Intraductal carcinoma is present at the margin  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  18 AUG 93 at 17 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 AUG 93 at 09 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 4cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm with ill defined borders grossly within 0 1cm of one inked margin  The lesion was too small to freeze  The lesion is submitted in A and B  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in C through G  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   SMALL SUSPICIOUS AREA  NOT LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE , Present.
