Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 32 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a breast lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm containing two sutures  A short suture designates the superior margin and a long suture designates the lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 3cm hemorrhagic biopsy site with an adjacent 1 4cm firm  tan white area grossly abutting the inked margins anteriorly  The biopsy site comes within 1 5cm of the deep margin which is overinked blue  The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is composed predominantly of dense  white  fibrous tissue with no additional anomalies  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  residue  B C  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest anterior margin  D  Biopsy cavity in relation to deep margin  inked blue   E  Remainder of biopsy cavity with adjacent firm nodule abutting anterior margin  F  Representative section of fibrous tissue from medial aspect  G  Representative section of fibrous tissue from lateral aspect  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are 3 additional specimens  Labeled  additional shaved margins  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  The specimens are sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes H through M  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a segment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassette N and O  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm segment of fatty adipose tissue  Numerous lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes P through S  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST LUMPECTOMY   MARGIN FREE OF TUMOR   NO TUMOR IN THE SECTION   O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGINS   EXCISIO PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL    EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Present.
