t breast  modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached 7 x 5 x 3cm axillary tail and an REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse with a 3 4cm diameter nipple areola complex  The skin shows no scars  The deep resection margin consists of smooth fascial plane  The side margins consist of unremarkable adipose tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is present  The specimen is inked  the axillary tail is amputated and the mastectomy is sectioned to reveal a dumb bell shaped firm  gritty  gray white lesion  spanning 5 2cm in greatest dimension  The lesion expands at both ends  2 4 x 1 3cm at the lateral aspect  REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm at the medial aspect   The mass comes to about 1cm from the anterior margin and 2 5cm from the deep margin  all other margins are more than 3 0cm away  The remainder of breast shows yellow  linear  dilated ducts leading the nipple and unremarkable pink fibrous breast tissue  SECTION CODE  A  Anteroinferior resection margin  B  Deep resection margin  C  tumor  lateral aspect D  tumor  medial aspect E  Dilated ducts near nipple F  Adjacent unremarkable breast  G K  Axillary lymph nodes  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 44 CLINICAL DATA  Lesion on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM MAXIMUM DIAMETER IN TISSUE SECTION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN O 2 CM OF A RESECTION MARGIN  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  All of the tumor is invasive  an in situ component is not observed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that staine