Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10 32 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast biopsy with needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA ARISING IN ASSOCIATION WITH DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  THE LATTER WITH APOCRINE FEATURES AND CALCIFICATIONS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size   0 1cm  Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma and spanning at least 1 8cm  Grade of the ductal carcinoma in situ  2 and 3  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Focally positive at the anterior and deep margins of the specimen  Stains for receptors  Requested  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 19 08                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block D   The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins  and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not contain invasive ductal carcinoma  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They