Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  RAD Mammography Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  CONNIE ROCHE  NP Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 59 year old woman with two left breast mass lesions  Lesion  1  specimen  A   is a BIRADS 5 on mammogram and U S and is located at 4 00 o clock  Lesion  2  specimen  B   is a 3 to 4cm heterogeneous mass on U S at 1 o clock  possibly a fibroadenoma  located at 1 00 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  see note   NOTE  The tumor is composed of large cells with abundant cytoplasm and fairly low nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio  The nuclei have irregular contours and hyperchromatic vesicular chromatin with prominent nucleoli  To confirm the diagnosis  we performed a panel of immunostains with the following results  STAIN TARGET RESULT E cadherin Ductal differentiation Positive Cytokeratin Epithelial cells Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive CDX 2 GI epithelium Negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Macrophages Negative TTF 1 Lung Thyroid Negative Vimentin Renal cell CA Negative The immunoperoxidase staining pattern supports the morphologic findings and overall  the findings are compatible with invasive ductal carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  1 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH HYALINIZED STROMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  see note   NOTE  The findings may not correlate with the clinical impression of a mass lesion  Clinical correlation to ensure adequate sampling of the targeted lesion is suggested  Multiple levels were examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  1 of 2  4 o clock   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  breast 1 o clock  2 of 2   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA  Recurrent breast cancer  stitch 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RECURRENT INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN SKIN AND SUBAREOLAR TISSUE  SEE NOTE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE REGION OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is noted in the dermis and subareolar region  All resection margins are negative for carcinoma  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 17 10                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16 19     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  This case is re examined at the request of Dr  Irene Kuter to establish the dimensions of the invasive component  The invasive tumor is present on 2 of 7 sections and is REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm as measured from slide A  It mostly involves the dermis of the nipple  The presence of ductal carcinoma in situ adjacent to the invasive component raises the possibility that this is a new primary tumor rather than a true recurrence  although the latter possibilty cannot be excluded  Lymphatic invasion is identified  but it is not extensive  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 02 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm tan skin ellipse  There is an eccentric 2 3cm areola with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm firm  flattened  tan red nipple  There is a 2 3cm scar arising 0 4cm superolateral to the nipple  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The resection margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 9 x 3 7cm region of dense gray white fibrosis with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm region of diffuse hemorrhage deep to the nipple which comes to 1 0cm of the superficial margin and 2 5cm of the deep margin  The remaining cut surface is 70  tan yellow lobular and 30  gray white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Hemorrhagic focus to nipple and deep margin B  Skin to hemorrhagic focus and superficial and deep margins C D  Hemorrhagic focus with surrounding fibrous tissue and skin E  Deep margin to hemorrhagic focus F G  Representative dense fibrous tissue away from hemorrhagic focus Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 57 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  98   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasions are not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast tissue fragment with a wire in place with accompanied x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with many small firm nodules scattered throughout  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  tan yellow stellate mass is identified  0 5cm from the inked resection margin  A representative section of the tumor is frozen as frozen section  1 save frozen  The mass is entirely in A through E  representative section of the remainder in F through J  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DCIS  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
